<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Details of Intervention Setting</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The intervention configurations used to obtain the results in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.3 Multilingual Generation Control ‣ 4 Experimental Settings ‣ Language Lives in Sparse Dimensions: Toward Interpretable and Efficient Multilingual Control for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> are: Llama2–7B—layer 19, <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.4</annotation></semantics></math> for monolingual and parallel; Llama2–13B—layer 19, <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.4</annotation></semantics></math> for monolingual and <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.3</annotation></semantics></math> for parallel; Llama3.1–8B—layer 21, <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.4</annotation></semantics></math> for monolingual and layer 27, <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.8</annotation></semantics></math> for parallel; Aya23–8B—layer 29, <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!1.2</annotation></semantics></math> for monolingual and layer 27, <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.8</annotation></semantics></math> for parallel.
The intervention layer and <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> are selected via a grid search</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Choosing an anchor layer for Llama2-13B</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Ablation on Llama2–13B shows that using layer 22 as the intermediate reference and contrasting it with the final layer yields the most effective set of language-specific dimensions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.07213v1/inter_llama13b.svg" id="A1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/307;" width="476" height="307"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Choosing an anchor layer for monolingual setting. Ablation on Llama2–13B in the monolingual setting.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Extra Experiments</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present grid search results over the intervention layer and the scaling coefficient <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for Llama2–7B in parallel setting, and Llama2–13B in monolingual and parallel settings.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the grid search, the optimal intervention settings are as follows: for Llama2–7B under the parallel setting, layer 19 with <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.4</annotation></semantics></math>; for Llama2–13B under the monolingual setting, layer 19 with <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.4</annotation></semantics></math>; for Llama2–13B under the parallel setting, layer 19 with <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F9.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.07213v1/acc_surface_llama7b_para.png" id="A1.F9.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/224;" width="476" height="224" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Overall ACC</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F9.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.07213v1/bleu_surface_llama7b_para.png" id="A1.F9.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/224;" width="476" height="224" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Overall BLEU</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F9.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.07213v1/combined_surface_llama7b_para.png" id="A1.F9.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/224;" width="476" height="224" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Overall ACC*BLEU</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Grid search results of Llama2-7B in parallel setting. The results show that the most effective intervention should be applied to layer 19, with <math id="A1.F9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.4</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F10.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.07213v1/acc_surface_llama13b_mono.png" id="A1.F10.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/224;" width="476" height="224" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Overall ACC</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F10.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.07213v1/bleu_surface_llama13b_mono.png" id="A1.F10.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/224;" width="476" height="224" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Overall BLEU</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F10.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.07213v1/combined_surface_llama13b_mono.png" id="A1.F10.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/224;" width="476" height="224" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Overall ACC*BLEU</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>Grid search results of Llama2-13B in monolingual setting. The results show that the most effective intervention should be applied to layer 19, with <math id="A1.F10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.4</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F11.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.07213v1/acc_surface_llama13b_para.png" id="A1.F11.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/224;" width="476" height="224" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Overall ACC</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F11.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.07213v1/bleu_surface_llama13b_para.png" id="A1.F11.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/224;" width="476" height="224" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Overall BLEU</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F11.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.07213v1/combined_surface_llama13b_para.png" id="A1.F11.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/224;" width="476" height="224" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Overall ACC*BLEU</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Grid search results of Llama2-13B in parallel setting. The results show that the most effective intervention should be applied to layer 19, with <math id="A1.F11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\!=\!0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\!=\!0.3</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite"><span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">*</span></cite></p>
